11
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:38.430
A pancreas that is connected to the liver and a dorsal pancreas,

12
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.810
which will make this whole movement and we see all this rotation that will happen at

13
00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.480
the same time.

14
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.490
This axis that will form here and it will place itself very posteriorly in a

15
00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:51.210
mesentery that we call posterior mesentery in relation to this hepatic rotation.

16
00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.030
If you understood yesterday this movement of development of the omental bursa,

17
00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.090
you begin to understand that all the rest is only a dynamic of this development,

18
00:00:59.090 --> 00:00:59.960
